# Cursor → server commands (user pastes them)

The user does **not** invent SSH steps. Whatever this chat prints, they run. Commands must be safe on live thenaradmuni.com.

**Always:** one recipe, full paths, labeled **as thenaradmuni** vs **as root**. If they are already `thenaradmuni@`, omit `su - thenaradmuni`. If they are `root@`, start with `su - thenaradmuni` except for `systemctl`.

**Never include:** `git checkout -- public_html/admin/config.php`, `git reset --hard`, `git stash`, `git clean`, `rm config.php`, or restart Next unless `web/` changed in that push.

Site: `/home/thenaradmuni/htdocs/www.thenaradmuni.com`

After every `git pull`, they must still see production config (`thenaradmuni.com`, `paldigitalnews`, `newssite3`). If `localhost` or `thenaradmunicom_db` appears, tell them **STOP** and fix File Manager — do not pull again.

## One-time lock (only if config is already production)

```bash
cd /home/thenaradmuni/htdocs/www.thenaradmuni.com
git update-index --assume-unchanged public_html/admin/config.php
```

Then `git pull` will not replace live `config.php`.

## Recipe A — PHP only (no files under `web/`)

```bash
cd /home/thenaradmuni/htdocs/www.thenaradmuni.com
grep -E 'urlroot|db_name|\$user' public_html/admin/config.php | head -5
git pull
grep -E 'urlroot|db_name|\$user' public_html/admin/config.php | head -5
```

Do **not** add `npm run build` or `systemctl restart`.

## Recipe B — `web/` changed

Block 1 (thenaradmuni) — wait for build **success**:

```bash
cd /home/thenaradmuni/htdocs/www.thenaradmuni.com
grep -E 'urlroot|db_name' public_html/admin/config.php | head -3
git pull
grep -E 'urlroot|db_name' public_html/admin/config.php | head -3
cd web && npm run build
```

Block 2 (**root** only, after build OK):

```bash
systemctl restart thenaradmuni-next
systemctl status thenaradmuni-next --no-pager
```

Brief 500 on the homepage during restart is expected. Admin 500 after Ready = config.php, not Next.

If both PHP and `web/` changed, use Recipe B once (pull gets both). Still never checkout `config.php`.
